{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_COM_SECTION_7_6_2_14_Service_0x2F_InputOutputControlByIdentifier","src":"manifest","doc":"SWS_DiagnosticCommunicationManager","page":169,"text":"7.6.2.14 Service 0x2F - InputOutputControlByIdentifier\n[SWS_Dcm_00256] ⌈The Dcm module shall implement the UDS Service InputOutput-\nControlByIdentifier (0x2F).⌋(RS_Diag_04218)\nWhen using Service 0x2F, the request of the tester contains a 2-byte DID.\nManager\nThe configuration of the Dcm contains a list of supported DID’s. For each DID, the Dcm\nconfiguration specifies:\n• The 2-bytes DID (see configuration parameter DcmDspDidIdentifier)\n• For every data of the DID :\n– The function Xxx_ReturnControlToECU() for this data (see configuration pa-\nrameters DcmDspDataReturnControlToEcuFnc and DcmDspDataUse-\nPort)\n– The function Xxx_ResetToDefault() for this data (see configuration parame-\nters DcmDspDataResetToDefaultFnc and DcmDspDataUsePort)\n– The function Xxx_FreezeCurrentState() for this DID (see configuration pa-\nrameters DcmDspDataFreezeCurrentStateFnc and DcmDspDataUse-\nPort)\n– The function Xxx_ShortTermAdjustment() for this DID (see configura-\ntion parameters DcmDspDataShortTermAdjustmentFnc and DcmDsp-\nDataUsePort)\n– The\nsizes\nof\nthe\ncontrol\nrecord\nused\nin\nthe\nfunction\nXxx_ShortTermAdjustment() (see configuration parameter and DcmD-\nspDataByteSize)\n[SWS_Dcm_00579] ⌈The Dcm shall support InputOutputControlParameter definitions\naccording to [SWS_Dcm_01661].⌋(RS_Diag_04218)\n[SWS_Dcm_01661] InputOutputControlParameter definitions ⌈\nHex\nDescription\n00\nreturnControlToECU\n01\nresetToDefault\n02\nfreezeCurrentState\n03\nshortTermAdjustment\nTable 7.23: InputOutputControlParameter definitions\n⌋()\n[SWS_Dcm_01554] IOControl DID authentication check ⌈On reception of the UDS\nService InputOutputControlByIdentifier (0x2F), the Dcm shall check if the control ac-\ncess to the requested DID is authenticated and control the IO only if:\n• for that IO control a role is configured via DcmDspDidControlRoleRef and the\nverification according to [SWS_Dcm_01522] was successful or\n• the active white list on that connection has for the requested DID one entry with\ncontrol access that matches that DID.…","caption":"7.6.2.14 Service 0x2F - InputOutputControlByIdentifier","sha":null,"series":[{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_COM_SECTION_7_6_2_14_Service_0x2F_InputOutputControlByIdentifier","releases":["R23-11"],"page":169,"hash":"70ee0927dc03523a","caption":"","screenshot_path":"_src/spec/snippets/assets/806c959f5e5d/page_169.webp"}],"releases":["R23-11"],"screenshot_path":"_src/spec/snippets/assets/806c959f5e5d/page_169.webp","trel":"R23-11","tstat":"section","drop":"R24-11","kind":"snippet","platform":"classic","targets":[{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_Dcm_00256] im Text von SWS_DiagnosticCommunicationManager.","rel":["R23-11"],"id":"SWS_Dcm_00256"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_Dcm_00396] im Text von SWS_DiagnosticCommunicationManager.","rel":["R23-11"],"id":"SWS_Dcm_00396"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_Dcm_00397] im Text von SWS_DiagnosticCommunicationManager.","rel":["R23-11"],"id":"SWS_Dcm_00397"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_Dcm_00398] im Text von SWS_DiagnosticCommunicationManager.","rel":["R23-11"],"id":"SWS_Dcm_00398"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_Dcm_00399] im Text von SWS_DiagnosticCommunicationManager.","rel":["R23-11"],"id":"SWS_Dcm_00399"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_Dcm_00563] im Text von SWS_DiagnosticCommunicationManager.","rel":["R23-11"],"id":"SWS_Dcm_00563"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFER